# Flutter Screen Rules

## File Location

```
lib/screens/
├── auth/           — sign-in, sign-up, phone auth
├── onboarding/     — new-user onboarding wizard
├── wizard/         — goal/habit creation wizard
├── journal/        — journal entries & mood
├── presets/        — skincare, meals, workout presets
├── templates/      — template management
└── <feature>/      — new feature screens
```

## Scaffold Pattern

```dart
@override
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  final isDark = Theme.of(context).brightness == Brightness.dark;
  final colorScheme = Theme.of(context).colorScheme;

  return Scaffold(
    backgroundColor: colorScheme.surface,
    appBar: AppBar(
      title: Text('Screen Title', style: AppTypography.heading2(context)),
      backgroundColor: Colors.transparent,
      foregroundColor: colorScheme.onSurface,
      surfaceTintColor: Colors.transparent,
      scrolledUnderElevation: 0,
    ),
    body: Container(
      decoration: AppColors.skyDecoration(isDark: isDark),
      child: SafeArea(
        child: /* content */,
      ),
    ),
  );
}
```

## Orientation

**Portrait only.** Do not use `Orientation.landscape`, `MediaQuery` landscape breakpoints, or landscape-specific layouts.

## State Management

- Use `StatefulWidget` + `setState` for local screen state
- No Riverpod, Bloc, or GetX
- For persistence, use `SharedPreferences` via service static methods

## Navigation

```dart
Navigator.of(context).push(MaterialPageRoute(builder: (_) => const NextScreen()));
Navigator.of(context).pop();
```

No named routes unless already present in `main.dart`.

## Loading States

```dart
if (_isLoading) {
  return const Center(
    child: CircularProgressIndicator(),
  );
}
```

Use `colorScheme.primary` for progress indicators (automatic with Material 3).

## Error States

Display inline, not via `SnackBar` for persistent errors:
```dart
Text('Something went wrong.', style: AppTypography.error(context))
```

Use `SnackBar` only for transient confirmations.

## Best-effort Async (non-blocking)

```dart
unawaited(SomeService.refresh(prefs: prefs).catchError((_) {}));
```

Never `await` fire-and-forget tasks that could block the UI.

## Colour & Spacing

Follow `morning-garden-colors` and `flutter-typography` rules — no raw hex, no hardcoded spacing.
